{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "mosart_subnetwork",
  "description": "MOSART subnetwork (tributary) routing step (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the per-cell Euler step 2 of mosart_physics.F90:Euler (F90:114-132) composed of subnetworkRouting (F90:243-269) and updateState_subnetwork (F90:364-381), written as a storage ODE with the pointwise laws imported from ./mosart_templates.esm. Equations, exactly as in the Fortran: with no tributaries (tlen <= hlen) the subnetwork passes the inflow straight through, etout = -etin (F90:250-252); otherwise the Manning velocity vt = CRVRMAN_nosqrt(tslpsqrt, nt, rt) (F90:253) and etout = -vt*mt (F90:254), with the dry-cell clamp etout = -(etin + wt/localdelt) when wt + (etin + etout)*localdelt < TINYVALUE (F90:255-260), in which case vt = -etout/mt when mt > 0 (F90:257-259); dwt = etin + etout (F90:262); d(wt)/dt = dwt (the storage advance wt += dwt*localdelt, F90:123, in continuous limit); updateState_subnetwork (F90:370-380) sets mt = GRMR(wt, tlen), yt = GRHT(mt, twidth), pt = GRPT(yt, twidth), rt = GRRR(mt, pt) when tlen > 0 and wt > 0, and zeroes all four otherwise; and the lateral outflow to the main channel erlateral = -etout (the per-substep accumulation and averaging of F90:125-127, in continuous limit). Units per mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90 / mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90: wt [m3]; etin, etout, dwt, erlateral [m3/s]; vt [m/s]; mt [m2]; yt, rt, pt [m]; tslpsqrt [1]; tlen, hlen, twidth [m]; nt is the subnetwork Manning roughness (SI dimension s/m^(1/3)); localdelt = Tctl%DeltaT/DLevelH2R/numDT_t(nr) (F90:120). One deliberate divergence, documented for reviewers: when tlen <= hlen the Fortran leaves vt stale (it is unused in that branch) while here vt always takes the Manning value; and when the dry-cell clamp fires with mt <= 0 the Fortran also leaves vt at the Manning value, which is what the ifelse expresses. The tests block pins the geometry chain GRMR/GRHT/GRPT/GRRR pointwise (instantaneous tests, time_span {0,0}) and the one-substep storage traces in the continuous-ODE form, with numeric tuples from the stage-1 instrumentation dumps (stage1/dumps/mosart/gr_subnet.csv, crvrman_trib.csv, mosart_euler.csv); the trace assertions carry the measured Euler-vs-continuous scheme gaps (see README.md (Testing)). Reference: stage1/cesm/components/mosart/src/riverroute/mosart_physics.F90 (mosart1.1.13).",
   "tags": [
    "environmental_transport",
    "mosart",
    "river-routing",
    "hydrology",
    "subnetwork",
    "tributary",
    "manning",
    "cesm"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-26T00:00:00Z",
   "authors": [
    "EqESM project contributors"
   ],
   "references": [
    {
     "citation": "Li, H., Wigmosta, M. S., Wu, H., Huang, M., Ke, Y., Coleman, A. M., and Leung, L. R. (2013). A physically based runoff routing model for land surface and earth system models. Journal of Hydrometeorology, 14(3), 808-828. The MOSART (Model for Scale Adaptive River Transport) routing scheme these components transcribe.",
     "doi": "10.1175/JHM-D-12-015.1"
    },
    {
     "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM, cesm3.0-alphabranch: MOSART river-routing source (mosart1.1.13) - mosart_physics.F90, mosart_driver.F90, mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90, mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90, rof_comp_nuopc/rof_import_export.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
     "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
    },
    {
     "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
     "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
    }
   ]
 },
 "models": {
  "Subnetwork": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "./mosart_templates.esm" }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "wt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "storage of surface water in the subnetwork (TRunoff%wt), [m3]"
    },
    "dwt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "change of subnetwork water storage (TRunoff%dwt) = etin + etout; the Fortran type comment says [m3] but the code assigns etin + etout [m3/s] and advances wt += dwt*localdelt, so the rate reading is the code's, [m3/s]"
    },
    "etout_manning": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "unclamped discharge from the subnetwork into the main reach, -vt*mt, [m3/s]"
    },
    "etout": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "discharge from the subnetwork into the main reach after the no-tributary branch and the dry-cell clamp (TRunoff%etout), [m3/s]"
    },
    "vt_manning": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Manning velocity of the tributary flow CRVRMAN_nosqrt(tslpsqrt, nt, rt), [m/s]"
    },
    "vt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "tributary flow velocity (TRunoff%vt): -etout/mt when the dry-cell clamp fired and mt > 0, the Manning value otherwise, [m/s]"
    },
    "mt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2",
     "description": "wetted cross-section area of the subnetwork (TRunoff%mt), [m2]"
    },
    "yt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "water depth of the subnetwork (TRunoff%yt), [m]"
    },
    "pt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "wetted perimeter of the subnetwork (TRunoff%pt), [m]"
    },
    "rt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "hydraulic radius of the subnetwork (TRunoff%rt), [m]"
    },
    "erlateral": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "lateral flow from the subnetwork into the main reach (TRunoff%erlateral) = -etout, the per-substep accumulation of F90:125-127 in continuous limit, [m3/s]"
    },
    "etin": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "lateral inflow from the hillslope, including surface and subsurface runoff generation components (TRunoff%etin, computed by the hillslope step), [m3/s]"
    },
    "tslpsqrt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "sqrt of the average slope of the tributaries (TUnit%tslpsqrt, from frivinp tslp), [-]"
    },
    "nt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s/m^(1/3)",
     "default": 0.03,
     "description": "Manning's roughness of the subnetwork at the hillslope (TUnit%nt, from frivinp); network file stores a bare number; declared with its SI dimension s/m^(1/3) for dimensional consistency"
    },
    "tlen": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 1000.0,
     "description": "length of all sub-network reaches within the cell (TUnit%tlen, from frivinp), [m]"
    },
    "hlen": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 500.0,
     "description": "length of the hillslope within the cell (TUnit%hlen); the Fortran branch condition tlen <= hlen selects cells with no tributaries (F90:250), [m]"
    },
    "twidth": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "bankfull width of the sub-reach (TUnit%twidth, from frivinp twid), [m]"
    },
    "localdelt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s",
     "default": 180.0,
     "description": "local subnetwork substep = Tctl%DeltaT/DLevelH2R/numDT_t(nr) (F90:120), [s]"
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "vt_manning",
     "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "manning_velocity",
       "bindings": { "sqrtslp": "tslpsqrt", "n": "nt", "rr": "rt" } }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "etout_manning",
     "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [
       { "op": "-", "args": ["vt_manning"] },
       "mt" ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "etout",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "<=", "args": ["tlen", "hlen"] },
       { "op": "-", "args": ["etin"] },
       { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
         { "op": "<", "args": [
           { "op": "+", "args": [
             "wt",
             { "op": "*", "args": [
               { "op": "+", "args": ["etin", "etout_manning"] },
               "localdelt" ] } ] },
           1.0e-14 ] },
         { "op": "-", "args": [
           { "op": "+", "args": ["etin", { "op": "/", "args": ["wt", "localdelt"] }] } ] },
         "etout_manning"
       ] }
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vt",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["tlen", "hlen"] },
         { "op": "and", "args": [
           { "op": "<", "args": [
             { "op": "+", "args": [
               "wt",
               { "op": "*", "args": [
                 { "op": "+", "args": ["etin", "etout_manning"] },
                 "localdelt" ] } ] },
             1.0e-14 ] },
           { "op": ">", "args": ["mt", 0.0] } ] } ] },
       { "op": "/", "args": [
         { "op": "-", "args": ["etout"] },
         "mt" ] },
       "vt_manning"
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dwt",
     "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["etin", "etout"] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["wt"], "wrt": "t" },
     "rhs": "dwt"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "mt",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["tlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wt", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "wetted_area",
         "bindings": { "w": "wt", "len": "tlen" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "yt",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["tlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wt", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "rectangular_depth",
         "bindings": { "m": "mt", "twid": "twidth" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "pt",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["tlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wt", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "rectangular_perimeter",
         "bindings": { "h": "yt", "twid": "twidth" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "rt",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["tlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wt", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "hydraulic_radius",
         "bindings": { "m": "mt", "p": "pt" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "erlateral",
     "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["etout"] }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "geometry_chain_cell100312",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the subnetwork geometry chain GRMR/GRHT/GRPT/GRRR (mosart_physics.F90:441-497) from stage1/dumps/mosart/gr_subnet.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, k 4, gindex 100312): wt = 3.97311021312352278e-05 m3, tlen = 8.34171976659353095e+03 m, twidth = 8.16804371744665605e+03 m give mt = wt/tlen = 4.76293896737555222e-09 m2, yt = mt/twidth = 5.83118691835853067e-13 m, pt = twidth + 2*yt = 8.16804371744665696e+03 m, rt = mt/pt = 5.83118691835852966e-13 m (all above TINYVALUE, so every nonzero branch of the ifelse guards is exercised). The Fortran values are reproduced to round-off (rel 1e-12).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 3.973110213123523e-05
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 4.762938967375552e-09},
      {"variable": "yt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 5.831186918358531e-13},
      {"variable": "pt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8168.043717446657},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 5.83118691835853e-13}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "geometry_chain_cell101032",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the geometry chain from gr_subnet.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, k 4, gindex 101032), a narrower tributary: wt = 4.17603130711973979e-05 m3, tlen = 2.53029464608684866e+04 m, twidth = 1.96594306825645049e+03 m give mt = 1.65041305113539083e-09 m2, yt = 8.39501955974291802e-13 m, pt = 1.96594306825645208e+03 m, rt = 8.39501955974291095e-13 m (note rt differs from yt in the last two digits: the chain is not degenerate).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tlen": 25302.946460868487,
      "twidth": 1965.9430682564505
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 4.17603130711974e-05
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.6504130511353908e-09},
      {"variable": "yt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.395019559742918e-13},
      {"variable": "pt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1965.943068256452},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.395019559742911e-13}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "geometry_chain_tiny_depth_guard",
     "description": "TINYVALUE guard pin from gr_subnet.csv row (step 1, ns 2, m 5, k 4, gindex 100312): at wt = 2.93836914884621747e-07 m3 the chain computes mt = 3.52249803525364102e-11 m2 and yt = 4.31253572716525559e-15 m (mt > TINYVALUE so GRHT is taken, yt > 0), but yt <= TINYVALUE zeroes the wetted perimeter GRPT and hence the hydraulic radius GRRR: pt = 0 and rt = 0 exactly as in the Fortran (GRPT F90:471-479, GRRR F90:489-495).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 2.9383691488462175e-07
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 3.522498035253641e-11},
      {"variable": "yt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 4.3125357271652556e-15},
      {"variable": "pt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "geometry_chain_dry",
     "description": "Dry-cell guard pin from gr_subnet.csv row (step 0, ns 0, m 0, nt 1, gindex 100312): with wt = 0 the updateState_subnetwork guard (tlen > 0 and wt > 0) zeroes the whole geometry chain - mt = yt = pt = rt = 0 (F90:370-380).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 0.0
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "yt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "pt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "manning_velocity_cell100312",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the subnetwork Manning law CRVRMAN_nosqrt (F90:406-422) through the full geometry chain: crvrman_trib.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, k 4, gindex 100312) records rt = 5.81773231372646289e-13 m, vt = 1.38680929192335890e-08 m/s, mt = 4.75194918749198407e-09 m2 with tslpsqrt = 9.94987437106620021e-02, n_t = 5.00000007450580597e-02; the matching gr_subnet.csv row (k 3) carries the storage wt = 3.96394284671499548e-05 m3 that produces exactly that rt through GRMR/GRHT/GRPT/GRRR. The test sets wt and asserts both the chain output rt and the law output vt_manning (= the dump's vt; the dry-cell clamp does not fire at this storage), reproducing the Fortran to round-off.",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tslpsqrt": 0.099498743710662,
      "nt": 0.05000000074505806,
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 3.9639428467149955e-05
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 4.751949187491984e-09},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 5.817732313726463e-13},
      {"variable": "vt_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.3868092919233589e-08},
      {"variable": "vt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.3868092919233589e-08}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "manning_velocity_cell101032",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the Manning law from crvrman_trib.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, k 4, gindex 101032): rt = 8.37564932353432923e-13 m, vt = 2.51318221409314064e-09 m/s with tslpsqrt = 1.41421356237309507e-02, n_t = 5.00000007450580597e-02; the matching gr_subnet.csv row (k 3) gives wt = 4.16639574733840902e-05 m3, tlen = 2.53029464608684866e+04 m, twidth = 1.96594306825645049e+03 m.",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tslpsqrt": 0.01414213562373095,
      "nt": 0.05000000074505806,
      "tlen": 25302.946460868487,
      "twidth": 1965.9430682564505,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 4.166395747338409e-05
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.375649323534329e-13},
      {"variable": "vt_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.5131822140931406e-09},
      {"variable": "vt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.5131822140931406e-09}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "manning_velocity_dry_guard",
     "description": "Dry-cell law guard from crvrman_trib.csv row (step 1, ns 1, m 1, k 1, gindex 100312, clamped = 1): with wt = 0 the geometry chain zeroes mt and rt, the rr <= 0 guard zeroes the Manning velocity (vt_manning = 0), and the dry-cell clamp of subnetworkRouting (F90:255-260) fires (wt + (etin + etout)*localdelt = 0 < TINYVALUE) replacing etout by -(etin + wt/localdelt) = -0 and leaving vt at the Manning value 0 (mt <= 0 keeps the clamp's vt override off).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "tslpsqrt": 0.099498743710662,
      "nt": 0.05000000074505806,
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 0.0
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "vt_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "vt", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "etout", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "one_step_growth_step2_sub1",
     "description": "One-substep trace over [0, 3600] (one Euler substep = one DLevelH2R x numDT_t cascade): entry (step 2, ns 1, gindex 100312) wt = 1.22671012572302206e-06 m3 with etin = 5.09336561109318995e-10 m3/s (the substep's lateral inflow, mosart_euler.csv row (2,1,exit)); the exit state is wt = 3.06032174388425321e-06 m3. localdelt = 180 s = delt/DLevelH2R/numDT_t with DLevelH2R = 5 and numDT_t = 4 (the dump's 4 rows per (step,ns,m,gindex) key; phi_t < 10 in the CFL rule). The .esm integrates d(wt)/dt = etin + etout(wt) continuously while the Fortran left-sums the Manning outflow over 20 Euler substeps of 180 s; the measured scheme gap on wt (solver at reltol 1e-14) is ~6e-17 m3 abs = 2e-11 rel of the end state (the etout term is ~1e-8 of etin here) - the rel 1e-6 bound is 2-5x the measured gap. etout at time 0 pins the entry-state outflow = -1.88446035662946316e-19 m3/s (the value the Fortran's first sub-step evaluates).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 3600.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "etin": 5.09336561109319e-10,
      "tslpsqrt": 0.099498743710662,
      "nt": 0.05000000074505806,
      "tlen": 8341.719766593531,
      "twidth": 8168.043717446656,
      "hlen": 500.0,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wt": 1.226710125723022e-06
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-06, "abs": 1e-15},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "wt", "time": 3600.0, "expected": 3.060321743884253e-06},
      {"variable": "etout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -1.8844603566294632e-19}
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
